WEBVTT

preparation-01
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.100
Begin by washing and drying your hands.

preparation-02
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:14.500
Switch on the BIO light and press the button five times to select the brightest light setting.

preparation-03
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.500
The device switches off automatically after ninety seconds.

preparation-04
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Place the BIO on your head and adjust the strap until it feels secure and comfortable.

preparation-05
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.700
Align the centre with your nose. Check the alignment using your thumb at arm's length, viewing with one eye at a time.

preparation-06
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:47.100
Eyepieces should angle outwards so they are at ninety degrees to your line of sight when looking slightly downwards.

sitting-01
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:59.900
Dilate the patient's pupils to obtain a full, wider view of the fundus.

sitting-02
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:08.500
Hold the condensing lens close to the eye, lift the upper lid and rest your other fingers gently on the brow and cheek.

sitting-03
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:16.300
Hold the lens at arm's length, aligned with the light and retina. Edge shadows mean poor alignment.

sitting-04
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.000
To examine the retinal edges, ask the patient to look in different directions.

sitting-05
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.700
If needed, use the patient's finger or thumb at arm's length as a fixation target.

sitting-06
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.200
After the macula, examine all four quadrants of the peripheral fundus.

indentation-01
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.000
First inform the patient that this may feel uncomfortable.

indentation-02
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.500
Ask the patient to look away from the area being examined, then position the indenter over that area.

indentation-03
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.000
Ask the patient to look towards the area being examined, then apply gentle pressure.

indentation-04
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.800
This is an example of examining the superior retina.

indentation-05
00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.200
Maintain alignment of the light, condensing lens and retina.

indentation-06
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:10.600
You should be able to examine the far periphery of the retina.
